WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.340
So I'm gonna f---ing bury you right here.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.940
But you'll be dead before
Stevie pulls your teeth.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.340
Accurate. He says, "All
right, take his teeth out."

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.880
Back in those days, they didn't have DNA.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.940
They would identify
bodies by dental records.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.350
My name is Mark Silverman,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.755
and I was involved in organized crime

00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:21.180
with the Italians and the Irish.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.445
Today we're going to be looking at

00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:24.940
some Irish mob movie scenes,

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.043
and we're going to
judge how real they are.

00:00:28.295 --> 00:00:29.803
What, did you get your period?

00:00:34.042 --> 00:00:34.875
[yells]

00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:35.716
F---!

00:00:37.261 --> 00:00:38.520
One thing about bars, too,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.650
is you always know
who's coming in and out.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.130
So you have a good idea
of the strangers in there

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.240
or if there's something
that doesn't look right.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.607
You can really find
out if somebody's there

00:00:47.607 --> 00:00:50.878
to infiltrate the bar or cause trouble.

00:00:50.878 --> 00:00:51.878
[screams]

00:00:51.878 --> 00:00:53.165
Are you still a cop?

00:00:53.165 --> 00:00:54.206
No!

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:56.650
That's a great scene.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.220
I could tell you one thing.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.990
And it struck me right away

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:01.530
when I saw the movie for the first time.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.510
The state police are not going to try

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:07.200
to put one of their own inside of a crew,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.010
especially a dangerous crew.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.634
That's why they recruit informants

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.117
or top-echelon informants,

00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:17.526
because the informants can walk
the walk and talk the talk.

00:01:17.526 --> 00:01:22.526
And I have never really seen

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:26.660
an undercover police
officer inside of a crew.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.245
A lot of people used to say, "Well,

00:01:28.245 --> 00:01:30.522
I know that guy's a cop
because of his shoes."

00:01:30.522 --> 00:01:34.752
I would say, "You don't
think that they know

00:01:34.752 --> 00:01:36.900
what shoes to wear and what not to wear?"

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.695
Yeah, always, always looking
over your shoulder for that.

00:01:40.695 --> 00:01:42.750
I saw a cop when I came in here,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.350
when I was pulling into the parking lot.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.280
I didn't miss that.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.230
But these days I don't
have to worry about it.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:48.910
Guys on the street like
me that are looking at it

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.710
and saying, "Wow, that's pretty good."

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.900
School's out.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.500
Thank you, Frank.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.318
Police corruption back
in the '80s and the '90s

00:02:03.318 --> 00:02:04.490
was rampant.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.473
Whitey Bulger certainly
wasn't the only guy

00:02:08.473 --> 00:02:11.540
that had the inside track
with some of the departments,

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.547
whether they be local or state or federal.

00:02:15.547 --> 00:02:16.770
Other guys, I mean,

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.430
you're not going to survive on the street

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.420
if you don't have friends
within law enforcement.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.580
And back then,

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.370
police didn't really make as
much money as they do today,

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.640
and they were much more easily corrupted.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.110
As we moved on to the 2000s,

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:34.770
I think that they got a
little more stringent.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.150
You know, they wanted to
eradicate organized crime.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.070
They wanted to just put that
final nail in the coffin,

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:41.910
which they claim to
have done several times.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.360
We're not even supposed
to be doing this s---

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.878
this close to Worcester.

00:02:45.878 --> 00:02:47.960
This side of Worcester.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:48.793
Says who?

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:50.933
Says him. Says Costello.

00:02:50.933 --> 00:02:52.310
This is very accurate.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.920
So, they're obviously nervous.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.660
It's all about territory.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:57.320
If you're dealing drugs,

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.880
doing any type of business
in somebody else's territory,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.280
you are absolutely open to discipline.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.060
However that discipline is carried out,

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.160
it depends on the severity of the action.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:11.158
Like, if you look at Medford, Somerville,

00:03:11.158 --> 00:03:14.321
Winter Hill, South Boston,

00:03:14.321 --> 00:03:15.421
you know who's who,

00:03:15.421 --> 00:03:16.804
and you know where you
should be doing things

00:03:16.804 --> 00:03:18.120
and where you shouldn't,

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.946
because if you don't,

00:03:19.946 --> 00:03:21.963
someone will get your
attention one way or another,

00:03:21.963 --> 00:03:23.229
and you probably won't like it.

00:03:23.229 --> 00:03:25.550
But that's what happens.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.472
You know, he's got some
real good scenes in there

00:03:27.472 --> 00:03:29.455
and a good storyline,

00:03:29.455 --> 00:03:31.671
so, yeah, I'd say it's pretty accurate.

00:03:31.671 --> 00:03:34.250
I'd give it a 7.

00:03:35.195 --> 00:03:38.747
Listen, I just want to stop
by and tell you myself.

00:03:39.789 --> 00:03:42.265
Producer: Is that the zip
code for South Boston?

00:03:42.265 --> 00:03:43.515
No it's Charlestown.

00:03:43.515 --> 00:03:45.924
Everybody has the Fighting Irish guy,

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:48.080
usually on their calf.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.570
You know what I mean?

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:52.648
And, you know, it's not really like

00:03:52.648 --> 00:03:55.473
a requirement or anything,
it's just that they're proud.

00:03:55.473 --> 00:03:56.647
I mean, and they should be.

00:03:56.647 --> 00:03:58.289
They're always going to
honor and respect it,

00:03:58.289 --> 00:03:59.790
where they come from.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.925
I think my guys can handle it without me.

00:04:02.925 --> 00:04:05.290
I wouldn't hire them without you.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.182
And I wouldn't hire you without them.

00:04:07.182 --> 00:04:08.720
You're a unit.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.270
Everybody in a crew has a role.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.540
Part of his crew is the bank-robbery crew,

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.203
he's not going to put
Joe Flipperhead on it.

00:04:14.203 --> 00:04:15.308
He's not going to do that.

00:04:15.308 --> 00:04:16.528
He's not going to hire
one without the other.

00:04:16.528 --> 00:04:17.564
They're going to do it together.

00:04:17.564 --> 00:04:19.343
They do it right, they do it well,

00:04:19.343 --> 00:04:21.276
they keep the money flowing.

00:04:21.276 --> 00:04:22.826
The Irish Mafia, I mean,

00:04:22.826 --> 00:04:26.967
they're loosely knit crews

00:04:26.967 --> 00:04:29.090
that don't necessarily follow

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:32.250
the pyramid of the structure of power

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.760
that the Italians have.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.750
You have your bookies, you
have your drug dealers,

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:36.950
you have your hijackers.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.810
Everybody has a role.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.090
But the earner,

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:44.360
the guy that's filling the
pockets of the higher-ups,

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.230
is the most important guy in that crew.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:52.036
Just out of respect, smooth things over,

00:04:52.036 --> 00:04:54.105
just take this for it. All right?

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.722
Not going to cut it.

00:04:56.722 --> 00:04:58.528
You're going to do what I ask.

00:04:58.528 --> 00:05:00.463
Yeah, he don't want his money.

00:05:00.463 --> 00:05:01.818
He's much more valuable to him

00:05:01.818 --> 00:05:04.026
continuing to make money.

00:05:04.026 --> 00:05:06.100
Your earners,

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:09.330
you will do anything to
keep them earning for you,

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.630
because they're hard to find.

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:11.940
Believe me when I tell you.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.191
There's a lot of
knuckleheads out there that,

00:05:14.191 --> 00:05:15.780
you put them on the street,

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:16.950
they last about a week.

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:18.920
It's like, in reality, too,

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:23.640
it's the old-timers that
really have the juice.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.310
I always respected the
old-timers more than anything,

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:29.210
because these guys have more
wisdom in their pinky finger

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.270
than the guys that are young.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.440
That's a 9.

00:05:40.755 --> 00:05:43.904
I think that's probably why
I haven't seen this movie,

00:05:43.904 --> 00:05:47.381
because that seems kind of crazy.

00:05:47.381 --> 00:05:49.400
Kind of elaborate to do a hit.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.440
I didn't know that mob hit men
were acrobats and stuntmen.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.630
It just seems like a
lot of unnecessary work

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.880
to get your message across.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.390
Our feet may swiftly
carry out Thy command.

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:02.298
So we shall flow a river forth to Thee,

00:06:02.298 --> 00:06:04.348
and teeming with souls shall it ever be.

00:06:04.348 --> 00:06:08.060
I don't know a lot of Irish
mobsters that talk like that.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.868
It's like a little bit
of, what, the brogue?

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:11.500
Most of them were born here.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:15.870
They don't come over from
Dublin or anything like that.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.833
Maybe I'm at 1 or 2.

00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:20.568
I'm not quite sure. It was long
time ago with that, but ...

00:06:20.568 --> 00:06:22.450
I'm giving it a 2.

00:06:24.928 --> 00:06:26.207
All right, that's enough.

00:06:27.498 --> 00:06:30.430
And just f---ing like
that, I was Winter Hill.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:33.130
So, a lot of people
believe that Whitey Bulger

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.730
was part of the Winter Hill gang.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:35.840
He was at the beginning.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:38.160
I don't think I would
ever say he was the leader

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:38.993
of the Winter Hill gang.

00:06:38.993 --> 00:06:40.841
He was the leader of the Bulger group,

00:06:40.841 --> 00:06:42.450
or whatever you want to call it.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.560
He was running with the
gangs in South Boston.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:45.730
There was a power struggle,

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:48.110
and they wanted to iron
out those problems,

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:52.337
and the ultimate result of it
was, "Hey, let's combine it."

00:06:52.337 --> 00:06:54.570
You know, "Why don't we
make ourselves strong?

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.710
Why don't we blend Southie and Winter Hill

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:58.750
and make it all one crew?"

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.270
And that's what they did.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.440
But in 1978,

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.410
all of a sudden this huge
indictment comes down

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:05.950
against the entire Winter Hill gang.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:09.975
I mean, guys like Whitey, Stevie,

00:07:09.975 --> 00:07:12.500
Howie, John Martorano.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:17.473
The who's who of the Irish Mafia in 1978.

00:07:17.473 --> 00:07:21.440
And it's funny because as
it was taking its course,

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.313
you know, these guys
either went on the lam

00:07:23.313 --> 00:07:27.000
or some of them went to
jail or were awaiting trial.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.625
All of a sudden,

00:07:28.625 --> 00:07:32.125
you hear the word
"unindicted co-conspirators"

00:07:32.125 --> 00:07:35.455
when it came to Steve
Flemmi and Whitey Bulger.

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.305
So an unindicted co-conspirator

00:07:37.305 --> 00:07:38.979
kind of raised a lot of antennas.

00:07:38.979 --> 00:07:42.160
And, again, that's where
people fail to realize,

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:46.510
is that once he eliminates Winter Hill,

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:49.350
he becomes the Bulger group.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.658
I told him everything.

00:07:50.658 --> 00:07:53.758
The IRA, Cahill, the whole bit.

00:07:53.758 --> 00:07:56.440
You'll be dead before
Stevie pulls your teeth.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.810
Accurate. Accurate.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.828
He says to Stevie Flemmi, he says,

00:08:00.828 --> 00:08:02.690
"All right, take his teeth out."

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:06.820
You know, back in those
days, they didn't have DNA,

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:11.210
so they would identify
bodies by dental records.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:12.757
I think in the movie too,

00:08:12.757 --> 00:08:17.010
they refer to a dumping ground

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:21.570
where they dumped a lot
of bodies. Quite a few.

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:24.170
I remember when the state
police were digging it up,

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:27.490
it was bad, really bad.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.140
I thought Depp was great.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:32.840
Everything down to the walk, to the eyes,

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.274
you know, Whitey had these eyes

00:08:34.274 --> 00:08:37.480
that were grayish blue

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:40.220
with, like, no emotion behind them.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:43.890
And I think you'll see a
lot of times in this movie

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.240
when they show the eyes,

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:47.748
like, they'll focus
specifically on the eyes.

00:08:48.873 --> 00:08:49.948
They looked pretty good.

00:08:49.948 --> 00:08:51.620
I'm giving this one an 8.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.750
I thought this one was gritty.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:54.970
It was raw.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.580
It was pretty accurate.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.004
Ever since you came in the restaurant,

00:08:59.004 --> 00:09:02.180
he can't stop yakking. It's
Smoochy this, Smoochy that.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:05.040
I always wore the Scally cap,

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.055
and I was kind of a tracksuit type of guy.

00:09:07.055 --> 00:09:10.010
Yeah, a lot of Irish guys wear them.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:13.020
It's not a requirement.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:14.168
I just liked them.

00:09:14.168 --> 00:09:15.630
You're a good boy, Mopes.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.530
Don't think we don't remember favors.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.400
You're welcome at our place
anytime. Come on, boys.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:23.370
The Irish will work with
anybody that's making money

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:24.449
that's willing to work with them.

00:09:24.449 --> 00:09:29.160
I mean, there was, like, a
big ethnic stew of people.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.117
You know, you didn't have to be

00:09:31.117 --> 00:09:36.017
a certain religion or,
like I said, ethnicity.

00:09:36.017 --> 00:09:37.183
There was Italians,

00:09:37.183 --> 00:09:39.360
there was Polish, there was Jewish.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:43.090
If you have talent, you can earn,

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:45.110
they don't really care
what your last name is

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.293
or what your religion is.

00:09:46.293 --> 00:09:47.459
You know, it's about money.

00:09:47.459 --> 00:09:51.340
You make the money, you can be as --

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.170
you know, you can be an atheist.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:55.963
I don't know. Maybe a 6,
5. Right around there.

00:09:58.754 --> 00:09:59.610
What the hell?

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.834
Transferring them to Rikers.

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:02.830
Sorry, baby.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.971
So, if a guy goes to jail,

00:10:04.971 --> 00:10:06.820
you know, I mean, he's risking that.

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:08.380
He's risking losing his family.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:11.893
We got our money. You know, our envelopes.

00:10:11.893 --> 00:10:13.100
Little Jackie: You're welcome.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:16.159
There was less in it than what
we were expecting, and ...

00:10:16.159 --> 00:10:17.130
So?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.490
Guys go to jail 10, 12, 14 years,

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.110
and they come out with nothing.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:23.810
And what they come out to is

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.520
most times their friends
have betrayed them

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.891
and taken over the
businesses that they had

00:10:27.891 --> 00:10:29.680
and never took care of them.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.275
Never went to their wife and said,

00:10:31.275 --> 00:10:34.630
"Hey, here's a little package." You know?

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.600
I mean, I think you
should take care of them.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.070
They're supposed to, but don't expect it.

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:42.070
You know, you see what this whole

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.940
organized-crime thing has become.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:48.600
Disloyalty, no honor
amongst thieves anymore.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.983
All everybody wants to do

00:10:51.983 --> 00:10:54.100
is look out for A No. 1.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.660
I left organized crime

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:59.400
because I saw the direction
that it was going.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.613
I saw guys that lost their families

00:11:02.613 --> 00:11:05.330
and were betrayed by their best friends,

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.910
and it was just too much.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:10.730
And I realized that I made the
wrong decisions in my life.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.095
Little Jackie: How much
were you expecting from me?

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.170
Payments are down.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:19.650
The collections are
down? Who's not paying?

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.225
Collections are always down.

00:11:21.225 --> 00:11:23.000
You know? I mean ...

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:26.033
Most mob guys are great actors,

00:11:26.033 --> 00:11:27.700
and their best performances

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.200
are when they're crying poor mouth.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:32.766
We know you did a score for $80,000,

00:11:32.766 --> 00:11:34.483
but you have no money.

00:11:34.483 --> 00:11:37.355
You know, you can't even buy
a cup of coffee. Come on.

00:11:37.355 --> 00:11:40.390
In that scene, where she
was asking for the money,

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:43.182
he's got the money, believe
me, but not giving it to her.

00:11:43.182 --> 00:11:45.102
You know, something maybe about a 5.

00:11:45.102 --> 00:11:46.558
Yeah here's a few bucks for you.

00:11:46.558 --> 00:11:47.912
You're lucky getting that.

00:11:47.912 --> 00:11:50.345
No, don't sit down here. Get over there.

00:11:50.345 --> 00:11:54.290
Nah, come on, sit down.
Man, I'm f---ing with you.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:55.709
Hey, can you get him a drink?

00:11:55.709 --> 00:11:56.734
We need to talk.

00:11:56.734 --> 00:11:58.400
I think it's a great scene.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.780
I really do.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.920
I mean, they're just hanging
out, having a few beers.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.920
It seemed like there were
other patrons in the place.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.167
You know, if you're in a mob bar

00:12:06.167 --> 00:12:07.460
or a social club or whatever,

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.052
sometimes they'll just
come over to the table

00:12:09.052 --> 00:12:10.480
and just whisper something in your ear

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.593
or just say, you know,

00:12:12.593 --> 00:12:14.890
"Come to the back room in 10
minutes. I got to talk to you."

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:17.580
You two are out there on your
own, and we don't see a dime?

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.560
We don't run around like a
couple of f---ing errand boys

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.585
for you for 15 years,

00:12:20.585 --> 00:12:22.460
and what do we have to
show for it? Nothing.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:27.310
I liked the way that the
boss let them know that,

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:29.070
you know, "Look, you guys got to kick up,"

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:31.510
and these guys are standing their ground,

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:34.290
saying, "Look, we do the scores, man."

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:35.900
You know, "I got kids to feed.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.870
What are we, errand boys?"

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:40.970
And obviously if they've
been doing it 15 years,

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:42.184
they're far from errand boys.

00:12:42.184 --> 00:12:45.790
Never tell how much money
you made on a score,

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.330
because, believe me,
people will chase you down.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.070
Like, I remember I specifically did one

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:52.220
that was really, really big,

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:55.120
and it was a windfall.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.770
And I had people coming
from every direction.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:01.430
As soon as someone hears
you did a big score in town,

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.890
they got their hand out.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:04.740
Most guys live score to score.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.998
If you hit a score,

00:13:06.998 --> 00:13:08.342
you want to take a little time off.

00:13:08.342 --> 00:13:10.247
You know, you got it. You got the money.

00:13:10.247 --> 00:13:11.721
We're not setting up IRAs.

00:13:11.721 --> 00:13:13.950
We're not diversifying
our stock portfolios.

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:15.433
We're not thinking about --

00:13:15.433 --> 00:13:16.928
we're thinking about today,

00:13:16.928 --> 00:13:18.450
we're thinking about spending that money,

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.950
because we know that once we run out,

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.180
let's go out and do another one.

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:25.490
You know, it's not a long-term business

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:28.100
that you can retire from.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.370
That's why you see guys out there

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:34.140
that are 75, 80 years old
that are still hustling.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.160
I'm going to go probably 8.5.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.570
I really liked this.

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:38.430
Thanks for watching.

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:40.980
And if you enjoyed the
video, click the link above.

